Z||000000||GT Bastard||04-13-2000||01:48 PM||||I'm looking for a nice clutch for my 4sp conversion, and I'm interesting in the one you're currently running.  I found an internet site for ACT, but they didn't have any clutches listed for the Fiero.  Which one did you use, and did you buy it directly from them?  thanks man!  Oh yeah, what's your overall opinion of it?||||reg||4
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-13-2000||03:00 PM||||Sorry for the delay and lack of responces I've spent the last few days at Disney World... and on the sunny beaches of Pinellas county! (Tampa)   I Bought the Disc and the pressure plate from them but paid a fortune; and have since found a cheaper more drivable way to do the SUPER sticky clutch. BlackGT (Todd Green), I, along with the guys at the shop,( <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  ) and with a little help from my buddies at NAPA <A HREF="http://www.napaonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.napaonline.com</A>  ... figured this out. Get an ACT 4 puck disc and run the STOCK pressure plate. Todds car is SUPER easy to drive and even easier to light up the tires! Hes running a really hard 380 treadwear Falken tire and can chirp his tires at 80+ into 4th! with the stock pressure plate you can still drive the car in traffic and RAIL on it at the Drag strip. You MUST have either aluminum or poly cradle mount along with the rear trailing arm bushings. shifting agressivly will cause them to fail over a short time. (at least mine did, so have todds cradle bushings...still running stockys though) part# 7-502 at <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  or 770-434-0200 ask for Chris (Smokin Boy). you'll save about $30 over the fiero store. another option is to go to <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>  and get a 6 puck. Their 6 puck will slip better in traffic and won't shake your dash upon engagement. still running a NEW stock pressure plate, and bearing. I love my 4 puck and 1100lb pressure plate.. I hate it in traffice cause my CDs skip and the dash bounces about 3". Todds does neither of these... and was about 1/2 the price... the Pressure plate i like $58 retail.. $20 for the bearing and  $60 for the clutchnet unit... (ACT gets their center hubs from clutchnet... but bonds their own pads to a extruded aluminum disc instead of stamped,multi-ply steel) the Clutchnet ones are stronger but my ACT is about 2 lbs lighter... I'll get ya a pick of Todds. and mine.. just to show the difference... it will be in the morning though... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-13-2000||07:32 PM||||Thanks for the great info.  I think I'm going with the stock pressure plate and the 4-puck unit.  What are the PN#'s?  Is all the stuff at clutchnet.com ACT?||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||04-14-2000||08:26 AM||||no... only SOME center hubs are purchased from them by ACT. the disc and pads are made by ACT... Advanced Clutch Technologys makes the hubs that sell a lot.. Civic, Supra, etc. but the low production and steep cost of a Fiero hub would make our price about $500 for the disc since they don't sell any.. they have sold 5 I've bought 2! Luckily clutchnet keeps this stuff in stock which makes their prices SUPER LOW! ACTs friction pads are different from Clutchnets. Clutchnet has metal chips embedded into the ceramic, ACTS have the same chips , and cindered ceramic, but an extra additive for increased friction. I'm not sure what it is... but it makes the WHOLE car shake upon engagement. I'll get you a part # and post it in an hour or so.. I have to call the shop... they don't open till 9... it's only 8:15... more to follow soon... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||04-14-2000||08:44 AM||||Did you order it off ACT's website?  I didn't see any mention of the Fiero there.  Maybe I had the wrong address?  Do you happen to know it off hand?  thanks for all your help, man.||||reg||1
